# The timers, status and IRQ line. Timer A counts 0x10 (high 8 bits) and 0x11
# (low 2) against 1024, timer B 0x12 against 256 in steps of 16. 0x14 loads
# them (bits 0 and 1), enables their flags (bits 2 and 3) and resets them
# (bits 4 and 5). Status reads land around each expiry and straight after a
# write, which shows the busy bit; offset 0 reads 0xFF. Then CSM (bit 7):
# every timer A expiry keys every channel on.
